<title>AUSTRALIA: TENNIS-AUSTRALIA CLINCH DAVIS CUP QUARTER FINAL.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-AUSTRALIA CLINCH DAVIS CUP QUARTER FINAL.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE, Australia 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia took a wining 3-0 lead in the Davis Cup quater final against the Czech Republic by winning the doubles rubber at Memorial Drive on Saturday.</p>
<p>Result:</p>
<p>Todd Woodbridge and Mark Woodforde beat Martin Damm and David Rikl 4-6 6-1 7-5 6-4</p>
</text>
